Use reaction extent to connect species changes with conserved elements (@gc-extent: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @general-chemistry, #source "../sources/Chemistry-OpenStax.lingua#r_02Y5N2VMTTPBDSNYPD4Z26EZ94", #source "../sources/IUPAC-Green-Book.lingua#r_5SR8CP04E580VSV69MYQNSZ73F", #source "../sources/Chem1-Lower.lingua#r_0NFQA43WZVMECZY6SKZJMRXWBZ", #general-chemistry "Limiting-reactants-and-purity.lingua#r_0B70BWF6HF4MK461M5Q92HPSH9", #industrial-chemistry "../../industrial-chemistry/balances/Reaction-networks-extents-and-independent-constraints.lingua#r_25NVZFRFZNBVKYDCXPAA04Z95X") { r_5NMK6VYMTG3QWD994R4VPP4M1Y
**Read:** [Chemistry 2e — Flowers, Theopold, Langley, and Robinson](../sources/Chemistry-OpenStax.lingua#r_02Y5N2VMTTPBDSNYPD4Z26EZ94), chapter 4’s stoichiometry and examples; [Quantities, Units and Symbols in Physical Chemistry — IUPAC Green Book](../sources/IUPAC-Green-Book.lingua#r_5SR8CP04E580VSV69MYQNSZ73F), stoichiometry and extent definitions; [Chem1 General Chemistry Virtual Textbook — Stephen Lower](../sources/Chem1-Lower.lingua#r_0NFQA43WZVMECZY6SKZJMRXWBZ), reaction arithmetic and equilibrium preparation.

For one reaction with signed stoichiometric coefficients ν_i, write n_i = n_i,0 + ν_i ξ. Reactant coefficients are negative and product coefficients positive under this convention. The extent ξ has units of amount. Its allowed interval follows from nonnegative species amounts and the chosen initial state, before equilibrium or kinetics chooses what actually happens.

With hypothetical initial amounts 0.50 mol N₂, 1.20 mol H₂, and no NH₃, the reaction N₂ + 3H₂ → 2NH₃ has a forward extent no greater than 0.40 mol under the single-reaction closed-system model. At that limiting value it produces 0.80 mol NH₃ and leaves 0.10 mol N₂. This is a stoichiometric limit, not a prediction that a real synthesis reaches that state.

For several independent reactions, sum ν_ij ξ_j. Distinguish reaction, transfer, accumulation, and phase partition in a species balance. An element remains conserved across chemical reactions while a named species can be consumed or formed. A recycle affects individual equipment boundaries but cancels from a complete system boundary when consistently accounted for.

**Work:** derive the allowed extent interval from all species constraints, including an initial product. Confirm element and charge balances after a proposed change. Add a second independent reaction on paper and explain which additional observations are needed to determine both extents. Identify a balance that closes numerically but leaves the chemical interpretation underdetermined.

These relations become reusable foundations for process design, reaction equilibrium, electrochemistry, and metabolism. Later engineering will add continuous-flow, energy, and transport models. Here keep the distinction between possible composition changes and the physical conditions controlling them explicit.

